<workout_file>
    <author>Coach Claude</author>
    <name>Long Ride + 45min Race Power</name>
    <description>Sun Aug 23. SET FTP TO 185.

45min CONTINUOUS at 159W, then a 25min brick at 7:10/mi. Athlete's call to keep the full session rather than the softened version - and continuous is the better stimulus, since the race is 2h36 unbroken rather than intervals.

CONTEXT: Saturday was 15mi at 7:25/mi with 56min in Z4 (load 255). Friday was 2hr. Expect heavy legs. GATE: if the first 15min of the 45 reads RPE 8+, cut it to 30min. That is not failure, that is the gate working.

INDOOR because the drivetrain is still stuck. A 3hr outdoor ride locked in one gear on rolling terrain is not worth it. GET THE SHIFTING FIXED THIS WEEK - the Aug 29 race simulation has to be outdoors.

AERO IS THE POINT of the back half. You logged 85min in position Friday. Beat it today. Race day is 2h36 and that is where the last 2-3 minutes of the sub-5 bike split comes from.

GATE AT 45 MINUTES: if the legs are heavy, cut to 2h15 total and keep the 15min brick. Yesterday earns you that.

FUEL: 80-90g carb/hr, race nutrition only. This is gut training for race day's 90g/hr - three hours is the best chance you get to practise it before Aug 29.

HIDE THE HR FIELD. Watts and RPE.

NO COOLDOWN - deliberately. Race day T2 is ~2:30 and you run at race pace off race power; a spin-down teaches the legs to recover before running, which is the opposite of what a brick trains. The 60s at the end is unclip time and the shoe change is your transition.

AFTER: 25min brick at 7:10/mi, running inside 5min of stopping. If 7:10 is not there, run 7:20-7:30 rather than forcing it - the brick's value is leg turnover off the bike, not the number. Then 90g carb + 40g protein.</description>
    <sportType>bike</sportType>
    <tags>
        <tag name="endurance"/>
        <tag name="racepower"/>
        <tag name="703"/>
    </tags>
    <workout>
        <Warmup Duration="900" PowerLow="0.50" PowerHigh="0.73" Cadence="90">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="3hr: 2h10 Z2, then 45min CONTINUOUS at 159W aero. 25min brick after"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="120" message="Yesterday was 15mi at 7:25. Expect heavy. Gate at 45min"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="400" message="Start eating at minute 20 and every 20min after. 80-90g/hr"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="780" message="HIDE THE HR FIELD"/>
        </Warmup>

        <SteadyState Duration="1800" Power="0.75" Cadence="90">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="Z2 block 1 of 4. 139W. Should feel genuinely easy"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="300" message="EAT NOW. First 25g in"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="1500" message="45min gate: legs heavy? Cut to 2h15 total and keep the brick"/>
        </SteadyState>
        <SteadyState Duration="60" Power="0.75" Cadence="102">
            <textevent timeoffset="5" message="1min at 102rpm, same power. Smooth hips"/>
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="1740" Power="0.75" Cadence="90">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="Block 2 of 4. Get into aero and hold it as long as you can"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="600" message="Eat. Drink 500-750ml an hour"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="1500" message="1hr15 in. Fuelling on schedule?"/>
        </SteadyState>
        <SteadyState Duration="60" Power="0.75" Cadence="102">
            <textevent timeoffset="5" message="Spin-up 2. 102rpm"/>
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="1740" Power="0.75" Cadence="90">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="Block 3 of 4. Aero again. Log total time down today"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="600" message="Eat. You should be past 100g by now"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="1400" message="Halfway to the race-power set. Keep the position honest"/>
        </SteadyState>
        <SteadyState Duration="60" Power="0.75" Cadence="102">
            <textevent timeoffset="5" message="Spin-up 3"/>
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="1740" Power="0.75" Cadence="90">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="Block 4 of 4. Last Z2 block before the work"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="600" message="Eat now - you want fuel on board before the race-power blocks"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="1560" message="45min continuous next. 159W, full aero, RPE 6. Settle in"/>
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="2700" Power="0.86" Cadence="88">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="45min CONTINUOUS at 159W. FULL AERO. Settle, do not attack it"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="600" message="10min in. RPE 8+? Cut this to 30min. Otherwise carry on"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="1200" message="20min. Neck and shoulders talking yet? Stay down"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="1350" message="Halfway. This is the closest thing to race hour two you will do"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="1800" message="30min. Eat - you want fuel in before the run"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="2280" message="7min left. Hold the watts, hold the bars"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="2580" message="2min. Finish it in position"/>
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="60" Power="0.45" Cadence="80">
            <textevent timeoffset="5" message="GO. Unclip, shoes on, out the door. This is T2 - under 5min"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="30" message="25min at 7:10/mi. If not there, 7:20-7:30. LOG total aero time and grams of carb"/>
        </SteadyState>

    </workout>
</workout_file>
